From 5d64f3a9b5efb17e3b37279fd0eb66af4224be54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:57:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: bind MPEG geometry to completed picture epochs

Parser lookahead can publish a new sequence size before the final old
B picture completes. Bind dimensions to exact admitted sequence ranges
and the same packet offset used for the completed picture timestamp.

Publish changes in presentation order. Hold the first new-size picture,
append a real empty LAST after old-size pictures, and resume via START
only after LAST was dequeued. Keep fixed capture backing and reference
ownership; never overwrite a consumer-held surface or synthesize EOF.

Direct V4L2 and paired FFmpeg tests return all 108 MPEG1/MPEG2 pictures
through 320x240 to 640x360 to 320x240 with complete PTS and max pixel
difference 4. Both boundaries return LAST/EPIPE, early START is EBUSY,
and held exports remain unchanged. Prior corrupted 400-frame and clean
1080i 24-frame recovery regressions retain their verified output.

Change-Id: Id3a9be5edb113a0cc531a6d93912937623686f4d
---
